# Everything in this repo is read by bash, vim, ssh or git -- all of which
# either require LF or are happier with it. Git for Windows defaults
# core.autocrlf to true in its system config, which rewrites checkouts to CRLF
# and leaves every script here failing with `\r: command not found`. These
# rules override that per-file, whatever the local config says.
*           text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch the committed Mach-O binary.
scripts/repo-scanner binary

# Lockfiles and images are not ours to normalise.
*.lock      -text
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.gif       binary
